Z||000040||AusFiero||07-31-2001||11:46 PM||||Ok lets clarify a few things here.<BR>Yes late model MR2s are nice, only in turbo. I quite like them myself. Don't compare them to a 16 year old car though. Late model Fieros if still made would probably be factory V8 by now and would kick the ass of the MR2.<BR>I know my unmodified 86 GT can kick the ass of any unmodified 86 MR2 in this country.<BR>My insurance company valued my Fiero at $25,000. I can buy an 86 MR2 in Australia for under $5000 and my classic car insurance company would laugh at any MR2 trying to insure with them.<BR>My car attracts attention where ever it goes. 1986 MR2's are seen as sh1tboxes and most are running around with bits falling off them and rust hanging out of them everywhere. I live near the sea.<BR>Fieros are adaptable, brake conversions, new bodies, V8 engine swaps etc etc etc. I cant recall ever seeing a rebodied MR2 or one with a V8 in it. In fact I have seen many a Fiero here capable of eating Corvettes and Vipers for breakfast. I have yet to see an 80s MR2 able to do that.<BR>Fiero values are rising all the time, MR2s are not because they are a dime a dozen.<BR>Fieros V6s sound better than any 4 cylinder ever can. Well unless you like high revving buzzing noises. I don't.<BR>20 years from now I bet there are a lot more Fieros from the 80s still on the road than MR2s from the 80s.<BR>Fieros from the 80s look heaps nicer than 80s MR2s. Particularly the GTs<BR>As mentioned, second only in safety to Volvo the whole time they was made. MR2s are very weak in that department.<BR>Fiero owners have a real community and club thing happening that is going to last for years to come. MR2s from what I seen on their own message boards constantly brag how their MR2 is better then forum member B's MR2. And some of the misinformed sh1t I have seen posted about Fieros is laughable.<P>So when it comes to owning an adaptable, customisable car that is virtually indestructable. Tell me which is better. A 1984 to 1988 Fiero, or a 1984 to 1988 MR2? <P> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000041||Raptor13x||07-31-2001||11:54 PM||||I'm an MR2 owner, and yeah, MR-BAD is a moron. Ignore him.  I'm not trying to cause a problem here, but these are my thoughts:<P>mkii MR2s are far superior to Fieros, but they are a completely different class.  Its like comparing a Supra to an MR2.  I mean come on.  A good mkii MR2 costs 6000-16000 dollars, depending on year. Even a high priced Fiero shouldnt cost 6 grand.  <P>If you want to compare an MR2 to a Fiero, compare the mki MR2. They were designed as competitors to each other. The Fiero should beat it in acceleration, and the MR2 should win in handling.<P>A lot of MR2 owners dont like Fieros, but my belief is AT LEAST THEY HAVE THE ENGINE IN THE RIGHT PLACE!  They are also reasonably light.  Sure the handling is not what it should be for a mid engined car, but you slap in a big V8 and you have massive acceleration with still decent handling.||||reg||1
Z||000042||72vinman||07-31-2001||11:57 PM||||LMAO, Hey slammed that is too funny. All you need are some Playa' rims. I never knew a carpenter could make such a wicked spoiler.||||reg||14
Z||000043||Raptor13x||08-01-2001||12:01 AM||||Also, most mki MR2s are NOT RUSTED OUT SHITBOXES! Of course a lot of cars that are 15 years old are gonna be rusty, but there are just as many rusted Fieros and mki MR2s.  MR2s are extremely reliable, agile cars.  They are not built for straight line speed, they are built for cornering, and will kick the pants off of virtually any car on the road today in the corners.  And if you are gonna compare a V6 Fiero to an mki MR2, make sure you compare it to a supercharged MR2.  You have seemed to conveniently ignore that model.<P><BR>Most MR2 owners are extremely nice people, dont base your opinions of us on jackasses like MR-Bad||||reg||1
Z||000044||pityro||08-01-2001||12:17 AM||||hehe.  I need to get me one of those 2 liter bottles of NOS.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You guys know that MR-Bad really doesn't have an MR2.  That isn't even him in the pic. <P>Fieros are slick.  I drove one once, I just like the MR2 better.  I just like quality imports over american cars.  I also had a honduh once.  It was fun till this brick wall jumped out in front of me.  I may not like em but I have respect for some american cars.  hell my dads geo has over 250K miles on its original engine and still gets 45-50 MPG.  Too bad the engine was made in japan  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>92 Black MR2 NA||||reg||1
