Z||000047||pityro||08-01-2001||12:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Santa Cruzer:<BR><B>rotted out fiero's LMFAO there fiberglass and plastic you wanna show me a rotted out fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I will take my camera with me next time I go out.  Man there are so many nasty fieros around here.  Looks like rust.  I mean there are holes and creases and dents and what not all over the body.  I can't even tell the original color.  Saw an older one catch fire right in front of me once.  That was crazy.<P>Then again there is this yellow on that drives around here that is mint.  Looks like a newer model.   Very nice, the owner did a very good job of taking care of it.  I also see a white one around here.  Me and the driver always exchange glances and nod as we drive by each other.<BR><P>------------------<BR>92 Black MR2 NA||||reg||1
Z||000048||KEV||08-01-2001||12:37 AM||||The fiero has Plastic body panels not metal that rusts! I geuss you don't no much about fieros, so next time do some research before you open your mouth. Just to let you know you can up date the handling of the 84-87 to be as good as a mr2. I'm tried of people bad mouthing the fiero that have NO clue about the car, and only go by what they hear from someone that don't no a dame thing either. Don't just rely on what the press says about the car go drive one that has not been molsted. I've owned over 12 fiero's and loved everyone of them. So don't come over hear and bad mouth our cars, when you don't even own one or been in one. Mr-bad come over to Minn and lets run I know of about 6 people that would like to make you eat your words about bashing are cars! If you think you car beat a 400+hp fiero lets go!! There isn't a mr2 out there that could. <P>------------------<BR>BLACK85GT 3800V6 2"DROP, FLUSHMOUNT HEADLIGHTS AND WRAPAROUND WING||||reg||1
Z||000049||Formula88||08-01-2001||12:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Santa Cruzer:<BR><B>rotted out fiero's LMFAO there fiberglass and plastic you wanna show me a rotted out fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The space frame's steel, guy.  Steel can rust.  But thank you for playing.||||reg||1
Z||000050||AusFiero||08-01-2001||12:47 AM||||Hey raptor. I said I like late MR2s. Where I live I can justifiably say most 80s MR2s are RUSTED OUT SH1TBOXES (as you chose to yell it and all). Most of the late ones here even have problems with rust from what I have seen. In Comparison I drive a Fiero that lived its life in Canada, salt and snow, then came to Australia and lived near the sea all its life. I have only ever had to replace the lower radiator support bracket due to rust. MR2s are just another mass produced Japanese car not built to stand up to Australian conditions.  Any car enthusiast around my town would back me up. Even late model MR2 owners. On the owners being nice I am sure many are, they too are probably sick of all the ****  on MR2 forums and stay away.<P>Why do the MR2 forums seem to attract such idiots though that attack each other how their car is better because they have turbo kit X as apposed to intercooler B etc? Just a personal observation from having a look at a couple of them.<P>Oh I have also driven all model MR2s and they will not kick the pants off half the cars I have owned in cornering. They are nothing special at all. For the cost of a used MR2 Turbo here I can buy a good used Subaru WRX Turbo. Now that will kick the ass of any MR2 and is in the same price range in this country. How do I know that, because I have owned one and many other high performance cars. Stop overating the things and get on with your life.<P>I bought a Fiero for its sex appeal and good looks. Something a Japanese car does not have in Australia. We get models here you wouldn't even know about and trust me the MR2 does not rate high amongst them.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000051||DRH||08-01-2001||01:06 AM||||Fieros will rust underneath. It can get to the point here in the rust belt where they are no longer structurally sound. They don't rust anywhere you'd see without looking underneath though. <P>The shape any 13+ year old car is in depends a lot more on how it was taken care of than how well it was made. Fieros, especially the 4 cylinders, were marketed and sold as commuter cars and a lot of people are still using them for just that. People tend to see these as a way to get from A to B and don't take good care of them. The V6s and MR2s were seen as more of a sports car from the beginning. People tend to take better care of a car bought for this purpose.<P>There are a lot of crappy looking Fieros out there. Seems like most are 84s that someone is driving as their beater. One, or both headlights up, severely oxidized paint, some body panels with scratches, gouges or holes, etc... <P>Most V6 cars, especially fastbacks, I've seen are in good to excellent condition. Most of them seem to be owned by people that see them as more than basic transportation and try to take care of them.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000052||LT1 Chop Top||08-01-2001||01:32 AM||||Funny,....I cannot seem to get any of the MR2's (Honda's, Mitzu's) around here to have a go.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/chp4_2.jpg"> <P>Wonder why?????||||reg||1
Z||000053||Sleeper||08-01-2001||01:39 AM||||we're all in it together. we fix up our cars to our liking. Fieros and Mr2s are sorta similar and both can be fixed up <I>hella tight</I> . here are two prime examples, i've seen both up close and both are perfect.  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mr2_6.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mr2motor.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mike%20Murphy.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/38turbo.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000054||Santa Cruzer||08-01-2001||01:43 AM||||well said AUS!<P>------------------<BR>BlOw bIg cHuNkS oF aMeRiCaN v6 YoU rIcE CrApEr'S! <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html</A> ||||reg||12
Z||000055||pityro||08-01-2001||01:49 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>Funny,....I cannot seem to get any of the MR2's (Honda's, Mitzu's) around here to have a go.....<P>Wonder why?????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Man I bet they think you have something other than a Fiero.  I don't get any ricers trying to get me to race either.  They don't seem to know what to think about the car.  Most people just stare.  I keep thinking I am going to cause an accident from the rubberneckers.  and mine isn't even the nicest MR2 around!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>About the rust thing, it may just be dirt or something but man it looks aweful. I feel sorry for the car.<P>I have heard of people dropping a MKII turbo engine into the MKI MR2.  Now thats over 200 HP in a car that weighs around 2000lbs.  If they go all out and do that I am sure they do the ussual upgrades and what not and are pushing around 300.  I would like to see that against a v6 modded Fiero.  That would be interesting.<P>------------------<BR>92 Black MR2 NA<p>[This message has been edited by pityro (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000056||Raptor13x||08-01-2001||01:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KEV:<BR><B>Just to let you know you can up date the handling of the 84-87 to be as good as a mr2. <P>If you think you car beat a 400+hp fiero lets go!! There isn't a mr2 out there that could. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, you can dump money into the handling and make it "as good as" an MR2, but if you put the same money into the MR2, it would still be far superior. You can have your quarter mile, I'll take the corners.<P>Oh, and about the 400+hp, you might want to do some research before you make comments like that.  There are quite a few MR2s that could destroy a 400hp Fiero.  It is very difficult to get an MR2 up to 400hp, but it has been done on numerous occasions.<P>I'll autocross against your 400hp Fiero any time.  I dont guarantee I'll win, but you will have one hell of a race on your hands.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000057||Raptor13x||08-01-2001||02:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Why do the MR2 forums seem to attract such idiots though that attack each other how their car is better because they have turbo kit X as apposed to intercooler B etc? Just a personal observation from having a look at a couple of them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We have a very civilized and fun forum at <A HREF="http://board.mr2pages.com" TARGET=_blank>http://board.mr2pages.com</A>   We do not attack each other for crap like that.  There are some extremely knowledgeable people on there too<P>||||reg||1
Z||000058||pityro||08-01-2001||02:05 AM||||Just curious.  What does a new clutch cost you guys, OEM or upgraded?  Say just for parts.<P>We do get idiots but apparently so does this board - MR-BAD.   Where is he anyway?  <P>------------------<BR>92 Black MR2 NA<p>[This message has been edited by pityro (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000059||b lo 0||08-01-2001||02:09 AM||||Coupla things-<P>1-It is SOO not fair to compare late models (MkII MR-2's, nice cars) to an 18-year old design.  For their day, Fiero's were WAAAY ahead of their time.  Maybe Mr-Bad would like to come down and race Travis at Road Atlanta-he has a mostly stock 2.8l (chuckles under breath)<P>2-I like MR2s.  It's the whole mid-engine thing.  I just like Fieros better, because you don't see them EVERY FRICKIN DAY.  I love to talk to MR2 owners.  I once had a Mk1 owner ogle my car and talk for about an hour in the Border's parking lot, and my car has primer spots all over it, and has been wet sanded (=no gloss).  I love having a Fiero because a lot of people have no idea what it is.  I once had a guy at a gas station ask to check out my motor (sounds sweet) and man, you shoulda seen his eyes bug out when I started walking around to the back of the car with my keys!  Sure, a turbo would kick my butt, but c'mon, toss me an N/A to eat any day!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000060||Raptor13x||08-01-2001||02:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Oh I have also driven all model MR2s and they will not kick the pants off half the cars I have owned in cornering. They are nothing special at all. For the cost of a used MR2 Turbo here I can buy a good used Subaru WRX Turbo. Now that will kick the ass of any MR2 and is in the same price range in this country. How do I know that, because I have owned one and many other high performance cars. Stop overating the things and get on with your life.<P>I bought a Fiero for its sex appeal and good looks. Something a Japanese car does not have in Australia. We get models here you wouldn't even know about and trust me the MR2 does not rate high amongst them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you have driven MR2s and were not impressed by the handling, you either dont know how to drive them properly, or you have a mental condition.  <P>Can you honestly and in good conscious say that the Fiero looks better than an mkii MR2?  I actually like fieros(I'm one of an extreme few who do), especially the fastbacks, but the MR2 just looks so much sexier.  And it doesnt have the cheesy Fiero interior, it has a beautiful wraparound cockpit design.<P>Dont claim I dont know jack about what cars you have down there.  I know quite a few people from australia, and yes you have some nice cars that we dont have down here. Damn I want an R34 Skyline  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The mkii MR2 is the best looking car you can buy for under $100,000 in the United States.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000061||Raptor13x||08-01-2001||02:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B><BR>2-I like MR2s.  It's the whole mid-engine thing.  I just like Fieros better, because you don't see them EVERY FRICKIN DAY.  I love to talk to MR2 owners.  I once had a Mk1 owner ogle my car and talk for about an hour in the Border's parking lot, and my car has primer spots all over it, and has been wet sanded (=no gloss).  I love having a Fiero because a lot of people have no idea what it is.  I once had a guy at a gas station ask to check out my motor (sounds sweet) and man, you shoulda seen his eyes bug out when I started walking around to the back of the car with my keys!  Sure, a turbo would kick my butt, but c'mon, toss me an N/A to eat any day!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn, where do you live?  I gotta get down there!  Fieros are a dime a dozen here in Michigan.  I see an average of 5-10 of them every single day.  I have only seen 10-15 MR2s in my ENTIRE LIFE!  I have honestly seen more Dodge Vipers and Lamborghini Diablos in my life than MR2s.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000062||Dave Gunsul||08-01-2001||03:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raptor13x:<BR><B> <P>Can you honestly and in good conscious say that the Fiero looks better than an mkii MR2?  I actually like fieros(I'm one of an extreme few who do), especially the fastbacks, but the MR2 just looks so much sexier.  And it doesnt have the cheesy Fiero interior, it has a beautiful wraparound cockpit design.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is purely an opinion not a fact!<BR>I happen to think Fieros look far better than MR-2's.<P>Second: the Fiero can be made to handle just as well as an altered MR-2 can. Both cars offer quite a few suspension pieces and neither is superior once the aftermarket gets involved in the handling upgrades.<P>Now engine mods is where it gets a little foggy but it's pointless to argue about it anyway. You like your car better and we like <BR>our car better.<P>Now please stop cluttering up our board with this childish "my car is better than your car" crap!<BR>Jeez, next it'll be "my dad can beat up your dad"!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000063||Galen||08-01-2001||03:28 AM||||Dave, I can beat you up while my dad kicks your dads butt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>to the winner goes the spoils.. the others car hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"With one swift kick the door was off its hinges, and there he saw a god, but it was only a mirror"</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000064||onfire||08-01-2001||03:29 AM||||Where's Pearl Blue Soul when you need him?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000065||AusFiero||08-01-2001||05:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raptor13x:<BR><B> If you have driven MR2s and were not impressed by the handling, you either dont know how to drive them properly, or you have a mental condition.  <P>Can you honestly and in good conscious say that the Fiero looks better than an mkii MR2?  I actually like fieros(I'm one of an extreme few who do), especially the fastbacks, but the MR2 just looks so much sexier.  And it doesnt have the cheesy Fiero interior, it has a beautiful wraparound cockpit design.<P>Dont claim I dont know jack about what cars you have down there.  I know quite a few people from australia, and yes you have some nice cars that we dont have down here. Damn I want an R34 Skyline   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The mkii MR2 is the best looking car you can buy for under $100,000 in the United States.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Firstly I do know how to drive them. I flog the crap out of most cars I get into because I like driving cars to their limit. I also held the lap record at our local carting complex for many years so I think I kinda know how to drive. I have owned over 40 cars and most of them have been high performance sports machines. I have driven Ferraris, Lamborghinis, Porsches, Audis and probably most high performance cars on the world market. It used to be part of my job years ago.<P>I am sure many will agree with me that yes a Fiero does look better than any MR2 and more to the point is more adaptable if you want to change its looks and individualise it. I never said I dislike late MR2s, Fieros are just sexier looking in this country and as I have said all along, more adaptable to whatever you want them to be. MR2s dont get a second glance here. Never have and never will. Fieros often get mistaken for Ferraris outside of the USA. MR2s get mistaken for what?  Oh thats right Mazdas and Nissans. Why? because they are just another Japanese mass production car that look pretty much the same as all Japanese mass production cars. <P>Ok guys on here. Most of yous have seen my interior, does it look cheesy? <P>At least you show taste with a Skyline. They run rings around MR2s and Fieros. As they should with constant 4 wheel drive and the HP they have.<P>I wont even start to name the amount of USA cars under $100,000 that look better than the MR2. That comment has just proved how one eyed you are. <P>I have no more to say on this now as you came in looking for trouble. Now go back to your little MR2 forum and rave how good they are to somebody who cares. Oh thats right, most of them will *****  and tell you how their MR2 is better than yours.<P>Read the title at the top of the page. Pennocks FIERO forum. We have an off topic section for stuff like this if you hadn't noticed. And boy is this topic off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000066||87FieroGTx||08-01-2001||06:08 AM|||| Most people who say MR2's are better are talking about the newer MR2's, Now is it fair to compare a new MR2 to a 17 year old Fiero? I think not!<P> If it is to be fair lets compare the 80's MR2 to the 80's Fiero, In this case the Fiero is a much better car.<P> If GM kept making the fiero it would probably have a 3.4 TDC/3800 and a 6 speed manual by now.<P> I've had a mid 80's example of both cars and like the Fiero much better, And more than that I feel much safer in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000067||Formula||08-01-2001||07:31 AM||||best looking car under $100k......<BR>Vipers look better then an mr2,<BR>Corvettes look better then an mr2,<BR>Mustangs look better then an mr2,<BR>Firebirds look better then an mr2,<BR>Camaros look better then an mr2,<P>Those are all made in america too....<BR>if you want to get technical,<BR>Supra, NSX, Espirit, Carrera, Boxter, SLK, just to name a few...<P>This is my opinion though, so its cool if you think your car is the best looking car around..... a little bit egotistical but cool.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
