Z||000087||Ditz88GT||08-01-2001||05:05 PM||||Man, this is just crazy...I know there is a friendly rivalry, but this is just bad.  Here we are, both Fiero and MR-2 people, with really unique cars.  There was never a lot of Mid Engine cars, we should be happy we know something the rest of the car world missed, mid-engine rules.  I'm sure we could bash each other all day (and night) but the bottom line is we could probably learn a lot from each other.  I for one, would like to welcome the MR-2 people here, I would like to hear what they have to say.  But...I would rather not hear how "MR-2's rule and Fiero's suck!"  Nor do I believe they would what to hear the opposite from us on their board.  All I want to say is let's compare ideas, talk mods, stuff like that.  Let try not to bash each other, if there's any bashing, let's make fun of the poor people in the FWD cars!<P>Anyway, just my 2 cents<P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT<BR>http://go.to/fiero||||reg||4
Z||000088||VelociFero||08-01-2001||05:25 PM||||Formula:  Oh come on, how can you say the Mustang looks better than a MKII?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ?  I currently have 2 '00 model Mustangs as well as a Fiero and a MKII MR2 and I can honestly say I have had more thumbs up in the mid-engined cars than the Mustangs (I have had exactly ONE thumbs-up in a Mustang, and that was in the Silver one that my GF usually drives).  <P>Raptor:  you're preaching to the converted here.  Every one of these guys drives with the engine behind them; they know about handling.  It is true that my '86GT seems to handle "heavier" than my '91NA, but the difference isn't all that much considering the 5 year difference and the amount of mods (GT=mostly stock; MR2=literally $1000 has gone into the suspension *THIS PAST WEEK ALONE*)<P><BR>------------------<BR>1991 2.2L MR2<BR>1986 GT Fiero <BR>00 Mustang (Black)<BR>00 Mustang (Silver)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2pages.com/members/velocifero/SmallMR2one.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by VelociFero (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
