Z||000099||Cliff Pennock||08-01-2001||11:03 PM||||This is probably going to be considered blasphemous, but I too once considered buying an MR2.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Why? Pure and simple, Toyota has been making some very good cars the past decade and the MR2 is one of them. I've even owned a Celica for a while (together with my Fiero) and honestly, I enjoyed driving them both. I <B>do</B> prefer my Fiero over an MR2 but that's nothing more than personal preference. <P>So in the end, it really doesn't matter what kind of car you like, as long as you respect someone else's choice in cars. I prefer chicken over beef, but I don't go running to the <I>Beef Eater's Forum</I> and tell them how much beef stinks.<BR>||||reg||1
