Z||000106||Pontiaddict||08-02-2001||01:38 AM||||Hello MR-2 People.<BR>We pretty much knew how Mr-Bad was. Lately hasn't been much trouble until a few days ago. <BR>I'd like to add that Santa Cruizer is another misguided soul that doesn't know what he's talking about half the time. Feel free to try and ignore him. We do but it doesn't work most of the time.<P>I have to agree with Raptor about Fieros in Michigan. Being that they were all built here and alot of them were bought by GM employees, you do see alot of them around. Most of them aren't taken care of very well around here either and aren't much to look at. I've owned 2 of them and neither were very well maintained, my 84 was pretty rusty and that's why I got rid of it. My GT isn't as bad but it was the previous owners winter beater and it shows.<BR>There aren't alot of MR2's around either. I've only seen 2 or 3 of them myself. The thing is, they do look like about every other Japaneese car built.<BR>Fiero's aren't the greatest performers in the world, (I'd like to add, that it's the fault of GM and not Pontiac, a touchy subject for me so please don't go there.) but<BR>Pontiac did extremely well despite all of the crap they had to go through to even get the car built. MR2's were built with the blessing of the company and had more money put into it's performance and handling characteristics while Pontiac had to fight to make what they could get produced to work.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000107||87GTBro||08-02-2001||01:38 AM||||I think we need to start comparing apples to apples and oranges to oranges...<P>Don't go comparing a 1984 Fiero coupe to a 1996 supercharged MR2!!!  What kind of comparison is that!!!<P>If you are going to compare anything, make sure they are the same year AND the closest model.<P>IF pontiac had come out with a 1996 SC Fiero... I am sure it would have outdone a 1996 SC MR2...  Let's keep things straight guys...<P>How does the 84 coupe compare to the 84 mr2?  Someone do a comparison...  Which one has held up better over the years...  Make sure they have close to the same mileage on them too!||||reg||1
Z||000108||CUTTER||08-02-2001||01:54 AM||||I used to own a 87GT fiero and now own a 91 MR2 turbo. I personaly like the MR2 better as far as performance, handeling, looks, and reliability, but the v6 did sound meaner and the fiero GT did look more aggresive! My GT is now sitting in the bone yard! MR2 is now getting faster with a rebuilt motor hoping to run low-mid 13's. I know and still talk to fiero owners personaly and I still think they are ok, just would never buy one again!||||reg||1
Z||000109||uspspro2||08-02-2001||02:10 AM||||hey fiero guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>u know i almost bought a fiero V6 b4 i bought my mr2. I just like my car better, it's my opinion. You know, If I had bought the Fiero v6 instead, I am sure I'd be just as happy. I want to know about your cars I love learning about all cars. I think that we have the coolest 80's widely produced cars out there. Learning is cool, I'll give you guys an intersting fact. The Mr2 was released in 1984 in japan. Same year as the fiero. Don't say dumb things like we coppied your car. It's stupid. You actually think that toyota sat there and saw your car come out in 84 and said "OH we have to coppy that car!!!" and then come out with the finished product in a year. I love my car, I love your cars. There is just something about my car i like more. Fist off I love SUPER LIGHT WEIGHT, HIGH REVVING, and HIGH COMPRESSION NA's. Check My siggy. I am running 10.3:1 compression moddified JDM engine in my 85 NA Mr2. Just hope not all of you are so egocentric, that you REALLY think your car is far superior. The cars are well matched, One person may think the ponitac is a little better, one person may say the toyota. However, to say my car will eat your fiero for breakfast cuz it is 1000000000x better, is an invalid statement.<P>Marco<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://board.mr2pages.com/bulk/siggysp2.JPG"> ||||reg||14
