Z||000121||Raptor13x||08-02-2001||03:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ditz88GT:<BR><B>Man, this is just crazy...I know there is a friendly rivalry, but this is just bad.  Here we are, both Fiero and MR-2 people, with really unique cars.  There was never a lot of Mid Engine cars, we should be happy we know something the rest of the car world missed, mid-engine rules.  I'm sure we could bash each other all day (and night) but the bottom line is we could probably learn a lot from each other.  I for one, would like to welcome the MR-2 people here, I would like to hear what they have to say.  But...I would rather not hear how "MR-2's rule and Fiero's suck!"  Nor do I believe they would what to hear the opposite from us on their board.  All I want to say is let's compare ideas, talk mods, stuff like that.  Let try not to bash each other, if there's any bashing, let's make fun of the poor people in the FWD cars!<P>Anyway, just my 2 cents<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya know what, you have a really good point. I'd like to apologize to anyone I may have offended.  The only thing I really hate about fieros is all the people who put corny body kits on to pose as other cars.  Unique body kits are cool, but poser kits deserve a good ass kicking.  I'm sure a lot of you can back me up on this.<P>By the way, I dig the "chop top" look, or whatever you call the more sloped windshield.  It looks hella sweet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000122||Oreif||08-02-2001||03:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raptor13x:<BR><B> <P>Maybe I'm biased, maybe I'm egotistical, but I just love how my car looks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Since you like the looks of your car, Why don't you go back to your message board and post there? This is a "Fiero"  message board. It's funny how the first 3 threads are all about MR2's! The difference between Fiero's and MR2's is "Owner preference". In your previous post you say it's a fact that Fiero's are a joke, It is NOT a fact, It's the mis-informed that think that. <BR>Personally I have driven MR2's and I prefer a Fiero. It has nothing to do with how the cars handle or how fast they are, but for the overall feel of the car. Have you ever driven a Fiero? I have seen many posts in this thread that have so many incorrect idea's of what a Fiero is/is not. <P>Let's just call a truce. You go back to your message board and we'll stay on ours.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000123||Raptor13x||08-02-2001||03:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> <BR>Since you like the looks of your car, Why don't you go back to your message board and post there? This is a "Fiero"  message board. It's funny how the first 3 threads are all about MR2's! The difference between Fiero's and MR2's is "Owner preference". In your previous post you say it's a fact that Fiero's are a joke, It is NOT a fact, It's the mis-informed that think that. <BR>Personally I have driven MR2's and I prefer a Fiero. It has nothing to do with how the cars handle or how fast they are, but for the overall feel of the car. Have you ever driven a Fiero? I have seen many posts in this thread that have so many incorrect idea's of what a Fiero is/is not. <P>Let's just call a truce. You go back to your message board and we'll stay on ours.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, sorry about all my ranting, I get pissy when people insult the looks of my car.  The mustang comparison REALLY PISSED ME OFF.<P>There are just such a massive number of poorly maintained rusted out shitbox fieros in michigan its sickening. I never knew plastic could rust, but you'd be amazed how rusty some of these fieros around me look. From the sounds of it, they are kept in much better shape in other states/countries.<P>The well maintained fiero GTs are very nice, and even though I could never stomach the interior, 80s interiors are known for being horrible.  At least I've seen some nice interior kits that make the inside of the car look as modern as the outside. I like all the new innovations that Pontiac took to make the fiero, from the space frame, to the MR layout, to the plastic body, to having it not weigh 4500 pounds.  Thats almost blasphemy for the domestic market.  All very good things though.<P>Sorry if I'm being insulting, I have "issues" about GM, Ford, and Chrysler.  At least Pontiac made one car with the engine where it belongs.<P>I agree with the truce.  I almost decided to buy a Fiero, but the MR2 won my heart.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000124||87FieroGTx||08-02-2001||04:01 AM|||| As if bashing the fiero wasn't bad enough now these BOYS are bashing the forum!<P>I've got an Idea why don't we get the fastest 84-88 Fiero and fastest 84-88 MR2 and have a race?||||reg||1
Z||000125||Gragon||08-02-2001||06:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> As if bashing the fiero wasn't bad enough now these BOYS are bashing the forum!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Come on MR2 guys, you like your car for certain reasons, Fiero owners like their cars for other reasons.  If you want to argue the merits of the cars, lets do it on our own board and not clutter the Fiero board with it.  They want to talk about Fieros, not MR2s.<P>All of us have unique cars that we love, respect that and all is well.  No reason to start a rift between the two boards over one post by a trouble maker......<P>Thanks,<BR>MR2 Pages Administrator<P><P>------------------<BR>91 MR2 Turbo<BR>89 MR2 SC<BR>01 PT Cruiser||||reg||1
